ed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-14","committee":"Joint Cabinet Committee","time":"6.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Council","time":"2.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","time":"4.00 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 a.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","time":"10.00 a.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Environmental property service projected to overspend by \u00a3400,000","lead":"A \u00a3400,000 overspend on a \u00a3230,076 budget represents material cost control issues or unforeseen pressures. This scale of overspend will likely require reserve drawdown or additional borrowing, signaling financial management challenges that could affect the\u2026","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 1.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78385/78385.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Large Covid-era reserve (\u00a38.4m) still in reconciliation with unclear release timeline","lead":"A \u00a38.4m reserve held for an historical purpose creates balance sheet uncertainty; large releases or returns of unspent funding would materially impact the council's usable reserves position.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Business Rates Equalisation Reserve being drawn to manage rate stress","lead":"Reliance on the smoothing reserve signals weaker business rate income than budgeted, which could reflect economic stress in the district or changing rateable values.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 1.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78385/78385.pdf","headline":"Environmental property service projected to overspend by \u00a3400,000","detail":"The Property service under Head of Environmental and Neighbourhood Services has a budget of \u00a3230,076 for Period 1-4 but is already \u00a3103,913 over budget at month four. The service is projected to overspend by \u00a3400,000 for the full financial year 2026/27.","category":"overspend","matters":"A \u00a3400,000 overspend on a \u00a3230,076 budget represents material cost control issues or unforeseen pressures. This scale of overspend will likely require reserve drawdown or additional borrowing, signaling financial management challenges that could affect the council's financial position.","figures":"Service budget to Period 4: \u00a3230,076; Budget remaining: \u00a3104,793; Period 4 variance: +\u00a3103,913; Estimated 2026/27 outturn: +\u00a3400,000 overspend","quote":"Property 230,076 104,793 -2,068 -879 103,913 400,000","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","headline":"Large Covid-era reserve (\u00a38.4m) still in reconciliation with unclear release timeline","detail":"The council holds \u00a38.4m in Covid-19 funding relating to 2020/21 and 2021/22. This external reserve is not moving in 2026/27 but reconciliation and potential release is marked as in progress. Until resolved, this remains on the balance sheet but its ultimate destination is uncertain.","category":"reserves","matters":"A \u00a38.4m reserve held for an historical purpose creates balance sheet uncertainty; large releases or returns of unspent funding would materially impact the council's usable reserves position.","figures":"\u00a38,439,412 held, no movement forecast in 2026/27","quote":"Balance of Covid-19 income and expenditure relating to 2020/21 and 2021/22. Reconciliation and return/release in progress.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","headline":"Business Rates Equalisation Reserve being drawn to manage rate stress","detail":"The council forecasts drawing \u00a3325,000 from its business rate smoothing reserve for the remainder of 2026/27. This reserve exists to stabilise volatile business rate income. The drawdown suggests the council is forecasting business rate income below normal expectations.","category":"income","matters":"Reliance on the smoothing reserve signals weaker business rate income than budgeted, which could reflect economic stress in the district or changing rateable values.","figures":"Opening \u00a310,208,830, forecast movement -\u00a3325,000, ending \u00a39,883,830","quote":"Funding to smooth the volatility of business rate income.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","headline":"Local Government Reorganisation creates \u00a31m commitment for temporary restructuring staff","detail":"The council added \u00a31m to its LGR internal capacity reserve in budget setting to fund temporary staff in Legal, Finance and Human Resources to handle additional workload. The forecast shows \u00a31.124m will be drawn in 2026/27 to cover committed expenditure. A Cabinet report on the future structure is scheduled for October 2026.","category":"governance","matters":"This signals major structural change is imminent; the scale of temporary staffing costs indicates significant internal effort required for either merger, separation, or reorganisation, with uncertain duration.","figures":"\u00a31m added in budget setting, forecast expenditure \u00a31,124,279 in 2026/27, ending balance \u00a3609,196","quote":"To fund temporary staff to support the additional workload for internal support services including Legal, Finance and Human Resources. The forecast includes all committed expenditure.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Cabinet","paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 4.xlsx Period 1-4","paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78388/78388.pdf","headline":"Gateway site capital scheme requires \u00a31.5m new reserve funding and commits \u00a32.2m by year-end","detail":"The council has acquired a major development site (Gateway, Stratford-upon-Avon) in partnership with WMCA. It added \u00a31.5m to reserves in budget setting specifically for NNDR costs and site clearance, bringing the total committed to \u00a32.2m by 31 March 2027. A planning application for development has been submitted.","category":"capital","matters":"This is a material capital commitment with an external partner (WMCA); the council's obligations and timeline depend on the progress of planning approval and development, which carries execution risk.","figures":"Opening \u00a3970,980, MTFS addition \u00a31,500,000, forecast balance 31 March \u00a32,212,404","quote":"The Council has worked with the West Midlands Combined Authority to acquire the Gateway site located in Stratford-upon-Avon. This funding meets the Councils obligation under this agreement to cover the NNDR costs that may be due on the site until redevelopment. Additional funding was agreed as part of the budget setting process to clear the site, in order to progress the scheme.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-07"},"name":"Stratford-on-Avon","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Environmental property service projected to overspend by \u00a3400,000","lead":"A \u00a3400,000 overspend on a \u00a3230,076 budget represents material cost control issues or unforeseen pressures. This scale of overspend will likely require reserve drawdown or additional borrowing, signaling financial management challenges that could affect the\u2026","also":["17 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Standards Committee on 2026-09-21","n_findings":18,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Revenue Budget Monitoring Appendix 1.xlsx Period 1-4","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.stratford.gov.uk/documents/s78385/78385.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":45,"news_drafts_total":3}}